{
  "description": "Hash vectors for OID4VP transaction_data (EC TS12 payment SCA), OpenID4x profile Section 3.2.5. `raw` is the base64url string a verifier puts in the request's transaction_data array and `json` is what it decodes to. `hashes` is base64url(HASH(ASCII bytes of raw)) per OID4VP 1.0 Appendix B ('base64url decoding is not performed before hashing'), computed with Python hashlib, independent of any wallet or verifier. `noncanonical` marks entries whose JSON a re-serializer would not reproduce, so hashing a decoded-and-re-encoded object gives a different value. Vectors whose note starts HASH-ONLY have payloads that do NOT satisfy the TS12 payment schema (api/ts12-urn-eudi-sca-payment-1-data-model.json: amount is a number, payee requires name and id, transaction_id 1..36 characters, additionalProperties false); use them only to test hashing. The `conforming_*` vectors satisfy it and can drive end-to-end validation. These are not JSON-RPC conformance vectors and do not use vector-schema.json.",
